  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Australia seeks to change visa deal with UK after influx of Britons",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/nov/03/australia-seeks-to-change-visa-deal-uk",
      "description": "<p>Australia says easing of rules has led to surge in British visitor numbers, putting pressure on local workforce</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/nov/03/shabana-mahmood-migration-brexit-eu-labour-andy-burnham-kemi-badenoch-king-charles-commonwealth-uk-politics-latest-news\">UK politics live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>The Australian prime minister, Anthony Albanese, has told Andy Burnham he is looking at changing rules for British backpackers in Australia, after an increase in the number of travellers visiting popular hotspots such as Sydney.</p><p>Albanese, who met Burnham on Monday evening at the Commonwealth heads of government meeting (Chogm) in the Caribbean, told reporters he wanted to discuss changing the agreement between the UK and Australia that removes a regional work requirement for British travellers.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/nov/03/australia-seeks-to-change-visa-deal-uk\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-03T08:36:41"
    },
    {
      "title": "UK makes huge aid cuts to Commonwealth nations despite warm words at Chogm summit",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/03/uk-cuts-aid-commonwealth-countries-despite-warm-words-at-chogm-summit",
      "description": "<p>Nations in the group fare worse than others, with funding for nature projects especially hard hit even as climate crisis intensifies global need</p><p>The UK government has slashed overseas aid to Commonwealth countries, the Guardian can reveal, in contrast to the warm words for the group from King Charles and the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/02/andy-burnham-ask-countries-affected-uk-role-slavery-shape-formal-apology\">prime minister, Andy Burnham</a>, this week.</p><p>Amid sharp cuts in the UK’s aid budget overall, the Commonwealth has fared poorly, an analysis of the most recent and projected aid figures, seen by the Guardian, has shown.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/03/uk-cuts-aid-commonwealth-countries-despite-warm-words-at-chogm-summit\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-03T17:49:57"
    },
    {
      "title": "King tells Commonwealth leaders that Britain’s role in slave trade was ‘shameful’ but stops short of apology – as it happened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/nov/03/shabana-mahmood-migration-brexit-eu-labour-andy-burnham-kemi-badenoch-king-charles-commonwealth-uk-politics-latest-news",
      "description": "<p>Speech by Charles marks formal opening of Commonwealth Heads of Government Meeting (Chogm) in Antigua</p><p><em>Q: Do you think the UK should reconsider Commonwealth membership, given other countries just keep asking us for slavery reparations?</em></p><p><strong>Badenoch</strong> said she did not agree with that “because most Commonwealth countries aren’t doing this”.</p><p>China did all sorts of things. It’s not out there apologising.</p><p>The purpose of the apology is to make us look weak. It is to make this country look weak. And once we start looking weak, then we have every man and his dog making demands and sending us an invoice, which the British taxpayer has to pay.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/nov/03/shabana-mahmood-migration-brexit-eu-labour-andy-burnham-kemi-badenoch-king-charles-commonwealth-uk-politics-latest-news\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-03T17:30:19"
    }
